    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high offensive output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, who carry the highest efficiency scores of the day at 81.88 and 75.27, respectively. Both benefit from massive park factor upgrades and a favorable matchup against weak opposing arms\u2014Randy V\u00e1squez and Trey Gibson\u2014both of whom hold xERAs nearing 5.00. **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear priority, leveraging his #2 lineup spot and significant platoon advantage to anchor our production. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.33) remains a high-floor play against Luis Castillo, as his sprint speed and premium lineup placement mitigate the risk of facing a tougher arm.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Nasim Nunez** (51.58) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.77). **Nasim Nunez** was the closest to cracking the starting nine; while his elite SB potential is vital for our strategy, the optimizer favored the sheer run-production ceiling of **Miguel Andujar** and **Coby Mayo** against the soft matchup provided by Gibson and V\u00e1squez. **Sam Antonacci** (48.56) represents our highest risk today, as he draws the difficult assignment of Yoshinobu Yamamoto. While we value his speed and leadoff role, the 16-point SP skill penalty warns us that his efficiency may crater if he cannot manufacture baserunners against an elite arm. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as current projections rely on historical assumptions, and any shift in the batting order for **Liam Hicks** or **Curtis Mead** could necessitate adjustments to our daily game cap management.",
